      "text": "To determine the value of \\(v\\) for which \\(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\) is a root of the quadratic equation \\(5x^2 + 21x + v = 0\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Substitute the root into the equation:**\n   Since \\(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\) is a root, it must satisfy the equation. Therefore, we substitute \\(x = \\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\) into \\(5x^2 + 21x + v = 0\\):\n   \\[\n   5\\left(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right)^2 + 21\\left(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right) + v = 0.\n   \\]\n\n2. **Simplify the expression inside the equation:**\n   First, simplify \\(\\left(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right)^2\\):\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right)^2 = \\frac{(-21-\\sqrt{301})^2}{100} = \\frac{441 + 2 \\cdot 21 \\cdot \\sqrt{301} + 301}{100} = \\frac{742 + 42\\sqrt{301}}{100} = \\frac{371 + 21\\sqrt{301}}{50}.\n   \\]\n   Next, calculate \\(5\\left(\\frac{371 + 21\\sqrt{301}}{50}\\right)\\):\n   \\[\n   5 \\cdot \\frac{371 + 21\\sqrt{301}}{50} = \\frac{5(371 + 21\\sqrt{301})}{50} = \\frac{1855 + 105\\sqrt{301}}{50} = \\frac{371 + 21\\sqrt{301}}{10}.\n   \\]\n   Now, substitute this back into the expanded expression:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{371 + 21\\sqrt{301}}{10} + \\frac{21(-21-\\sqrt{301})}{10} + v = 0.\n   \\]\n   Simplify the second term:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{21(-21-\\sqrt{301})}{10} = \\frac{-441 - 21\\sqrt{301}}{10} = \\frac{-441 - 21\\sqrt{301}}{10}.\n   \\]\n   Combine the terms:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{371 + 21\\sqrt{301}}{10} + \\frac{-441 - 21\\sqrt{301}}{10} + v = \\frac{371 - 441}{10} + v = \\frac{-70}{10} + v = -7 + v.\n   \\]\n   Set the simplified expression equal to zero:\n   \\[\n   -7 + v = 0 \\implies v = 7.\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the real value of \\(v\\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
